1
00:00:25,511 --> 00:00:26,011
What’s that?

2
00:00:26,011 --> 00:00:29,014
Interior design for a coffee shop.
Isn’t it obvious?

3
00:00:29,014 --> 00:00:32,059
You notice everything.
Is something wrong?

4
00:00:32,059 --> 00:00:34,451
You’re just trying to
distract yourself, aren’t you?

5
00:00:34,456 --> 00:00:37,037
Why? Do you want to die? Huh?

6
00:00:37,042 --> 00:00:38,043
Kill me!

7
00:00:38,605 --> 00:00:40,857
Do you have plans for later?

8
00:00:45,808 --> 00:00:46,892
Like a pro.

9
00:00:48,102 --> 00:00:49,895
Looks like you’re enjoying
the company, huh?

10
00:00:49,895 --> 00:00:51,731
Well, well!
You’ve got an answer for everything.

11
00:00:53,395 --> 00:00:55,481
What? You want more?

12
00:00:58,097 --> 00:00:59,432
Sorry!

13
00:01:00,206 --> 00:01:01,165
Shan?!

14
00:01:01,818 --> 00:01:03,611
I knew it, you fucker!

15
00:01:09,116 --> 00:01:12,035
Long time no see!
Do you have a date?

16
00:01:13,672 --> 00:01:16,821
Now, the real question is...
why aren’t you following me back?

17
00:01:17,586 --> 00:01:19,320
You’re too close.

18
00:01:19,328 --> 00:01:21,219
So, just how close can we get, Kierra?

19
00:01:21,227 --> 00:01:22,270
Are you going to tell me?

20
00:02:52,687 --> 00:02:53,688
Got a headache?

21
00:02:54,314 --> 00:02:55,940
It will be gone later.

22
00:02:56,274 --> 00:02:59,027
You know you should eat first
and drink some water.

23
00:02:59,910 --> 00:03:00,785
I give up.

24
00:03:01,335 --> 00:03:01,794
Huh?

25
00:03:01,794 --> 00:03:03,522
I really can’t remember.

26
00:03:03,546 --> 00:03:04,922
Remember what?

27
00:03:05,860 --> 00:03:09,155
Luna, did you see any guy outside
the restaurant when we went home?

28
00:03:12,046 --> 00:03:13,255
I don’t think so.

29
00:03:13,257 --> 00:03:15,593
We only saw you dead drunk.

30
00:03:24,187 --> 00:03:26,397
I really feel like I said something.

31
00:03:26,900 --> 00:03:27,985
What do you mean?

32
00:03:29,394 --> 00:03:30,353
Nothing.

33
00:03:32,210 --> 00:03:33,587
Just eat.

34
00:03:35,116 --> 00:03:36,534
I can’t.

35
00:03:40,637 --> 00:03:41,346
Hey!

36
00:03:43,278 --> 00:03:46,156
That’s what you get
for drinking a lot. Geez.

37
00:03:56,820 --> 00:03:59,593
You know, Ke, don't think
about us too much.

38
00:03:59,601 --> 00:04:01,226
We're fine, okay.

39
00:04:01,242 --> 00:04:03,018
You wish. As if I’d think about you.

40
00:04:04,023 --> 00:04:06,413
Master, stop bothering her.

41
00:04:06,421 --> 00:04:09,195
She might be trying to
remember what she reviewed.

42
00:04:09,196 --> 00:04:11,407
Exactly, so annoying.
Such an attention-seeker.

43
00:04:11,408 --> 00:04:13,243
Are you actually trying to
remember what you reviewed?

44
00:04:14,617 --> 00:04:17,328
All right, get another barbecue.
It’s on me.

45
00:04:18,195 --> 00:04:20,140
You too, Theo, so you’ll finally shut up.

46
00:04:20,140 --> 00:04:23,805
My buddy is so generous.

47
00:04:23,812 --> 00:04:25,093
Make it two.

48
00:04:25,109 --> 00:04:26,993
- Oh.
- Huh?

49
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:28,602
- Come on, get this one.
- Okay. I thought—

50
00:04:28,609 --> 00:04:29,944
- you’ll eat it all.
- Let’s take a picture.

51
00:04:30,515 --> 00:04:31,855
So I can post it.

52
00:04:31,867 --> 00:04:33,345
Wow. Haven’t eaten enough yet?

53
00:04:33,369 --> 00:04:34,429
But it’s your treat.

54
00:04:34,453 --> 00:04:35,329
Okay.

55
00:04:36,007 --> 00:04:37,360
One, two, hey!

56
00:04:37,375 --> 00:04:38,626
- Theo. One, two, three.
- Oh!

57
00:04:40,074 --> 00:04:41,450
Okay.

58
00:04:42,585 --> 00:04:43,586
I’m uploading it, okay?

59
00:04:43,586 --> 00:04:46,339
<i>Got free barbecue from this doofus.</i>

60
00:04:46,339 --> 00:04:48,508
Hey, who are you calling a doofus?
Give those back.

61
00:04:48,508 --> 00:04:50,510
Hey, no! Don’t! I’m just kidding.

62
00:04:50,510 --> 00:04:52,428
- Change that.
- Yeah, I’ll change it now.

63
00:04:52,428 --> 00:04:53,280
See?

64
00:04:53,304 --> 00:04:55,181
<i>Got free barbecue from this hottie.</i>

65
00:04:55,181 --> 00:04:57,850
There you go.
Hottie, that’s right.

66
00:04:59,313 --> 00:05:00,481
- Hottie. - Hottie?

67
00:05:01,010 --> 00:05:01,844
Move.

68
00:05:07,096 --> 00:05:09,015
- Here. - Sir, one more, please.

69
00:05:10,485 --> 00:05:11,686
I’ll treat this round too.

70
00:05:11,695 --> 00:05:15,592
I’m so lucky with my friends,
they’re so generous!

71
00:05:15,616 --> 00:05:17,326
- How should I—
- My guy is such a show-off.

72
00:05:17,326 --> 00:05:19,319
Want to be called a hottie, too, huh?

73
00:05:19,328 --> 00:05:21,655
You really don’t get enough attention,
huh, Master?

74
00:05:21,656 --> 00:05:22,657
Don’t mind him.

75
00:05:22,657 --> 00:05:25,326
Let’s take a picture so
I can post one of you, too.

76
00:05:28,091 --> 00:05:29,134
There.

77
00:05:36,718 --> 00:05:38,053
When did I follow him?

78
00:05:38,642 --> 00:05:39,310
Who?

79
00:05:39,888 --> 00:05:41,265
Ah. Nothing.

80
00:05:41,710 --> 00:05:42,210
It’s nothing.

81
00:05:42,953 --> 00:05:45,998
By the way,
maybe you want to come with Sevi and me?

82
00:05:45,998 --> 00:05:49,008
We’re going to a coffee
shop down the street.

83
00:05:49,015 --> 00:05:51,195
- I’ll treat you.
- Yeah, it’s good there!

84
00:05:51,203 --> 00:05:53,289
- Coffee?
- That’s why I’m telling her.

85
00:05:53,289 --> 00:05:54,206
- Sorry. - Let’s go.

86
00:05:54,206 --> 00:05:56,887
You guys go ahead.
I still have somewhere to go.

87
00:05:56,911 --> 00:05:57,996
- You sure?
- Mhmm.

88
00:06:07,008 --> 00:06:08,510
- Thank you, ma’am.
- Thank you.

89
00:06:14,273 --> 00:06:16,312
Hello, Ma’am Kierra.
Welcome back.

90
00:06:16,328 --> 00:06:17,872
Having your usual Americano?

91
00:06:17,890 --> 00:06:19,421
Ah. Yes, yes.

92
00:06:19,429 --> 00:06:22,645
Where’s Shan, the other barista?
I just have something to ask.

93
00:06:22,646 --> 00:06:25,833
Oh, he's not here.
He’s not on shift today.

94
00:06:25,856 --> 00:06:27,483
Ah, I see.

95
00:06:28,481 --> 00:06:30,442
Okay, let me prepare your coffee.

96
00:06:34,299 --> 00:06:35,342
Thank you, ma’am.

97
00:06:36,503 --> 00:06:38,232
One Sakura latte, please.

98
00:06:38,234 --> 00:06:40,984
Ma’am, sorry.
We don’t have that on the menu.

99
00:06:40,992 --> 00:06:42,160
Ciandrei knows how to make it.

100
00:06:42,704 --> 00:06:44,081
He’s still not here right now.

101
00:06:47,351 --> 00:06:48,769
Uh…

102
00:06:48,769 --> 00:06:50,368
Okay, just an iced Americano then.

103
00:06:50,375 --> 00:06:51,523
One iced Americano.

104
00:06:51,524 --> 00:06:52,566
Okay, miss, coming right up.

105
00:07:05,050 --> 00:07:06,385
I wasn’t looking for him anyway.

106
00:07:07,010 --> 00:07:09,113
And you know, you guys
should just fire him.

107
00:07:09,125 --> 00:07:10,210
He never comes in.

108
00:07:10,703 --> 00:07:12,516
So, one iced Americano, miss?

109
00:07:12,523 --> 00:07:13,148
Yup.

110
00:07:18,113 --> 00:07:19,156
Thank you.

111
00:07:36,395 --> 00:07:38,772
Looks like he’s really busy.
He’s not showing up.

112
00:07:44,085 --> 00:07:47,641
<i>Ke! Where are you?</i>
<i>Let’s grab lunch in BGC?</i>

113
00:07:55,599 --> 00:07:57,450
Are you okay, Ke?

114
00:07:57,460 --> 00:07:58,502
How’s it going?

115
00:08:01,430 --> 00:08:02,661
Oh…

116
00:08:02,664 --> 00:08:05,208
About Dr. Bautista?

117
00:08:07,895 --> 00:08:11,315
I don’t see her anymore.

118
00:08:15,218 --> 00:08:19,431
I know another doctor. Dr. Peja.
Maybe she’d be better for you.

119
00:08:24,823 --> 00:08:26,867
Sam, do you know
someone named Ciandrei?

120
00:08:28,298 --> 00:08:30,384
Ciandrei? Wait.

121
00:08:35,011 --> 00:08:37,763
Wait. Are you talking about him?

122
00:08:38,610 --> 00:08:41,696
Why? What’s with Shan?
Is he flirting with you?

123
00:08:43,024 --> 00:08:45,025
He’s my friend but—

124
00:08:45,031 --> 00:08:47,992
You better be careful if you
don't want your heart broken.

125
00:08:49,006 --> 00:08:51,972
Why? Is he really a red flag?

126
00:08:51,984 --> 00:08:53,304
Does he never run out of FWBs?

127
00:08:53,304 --> 00:08:57,350
I can’t answer that. All I know is
he’s a walking heartbreak.

128
00:08:58,017 --> 00:09:00,579
You would think that he cares,
but he doesn’t.

129
00:09:00,603 --> 00:09:02,609
Well, Shan is actually kind.

130
00:09:02,625 --> 00:09:04,502
But he is like that to everyone.

131
00:09:04,507 --> 00:09:07,051
But there’s no chance
of commitment with him.

132
00:09:08,203 --> 00:09:09,537
Kind?

133
00:09:10,522 --> 00:09:11,717
Isn’t he leading them on?

134
00:09:12,344 --> 00:09:17,046
From what I heard, he tells them
upfront that he doesn’t commit.

135
00:09:17,070 --> 00:09:19,716
But the girls still fall for him anyway.

136
00:09:19,740 --> 00:09:26,014
He gives off this vibe as if you know him,
but the truth is you don’t.

137
00:09:26,038 --> 00:09:31,543
And you know what, he has walls around him
that only his closest friends can enter.

138
00:09:38,926 --> 00:09:41,164
Why? Is he your type?

139
00:09:41,171 --> 00:09:42,832
No, yuck. He’s not.

140
00:09:42,856 --> 00:09:47,677
I just asked because I see him at
the coffee shop, working as a barista.

141
00:09:48,339 --> 00:09:49,715
Oh, he owns that.

142
00:09:50,226 --> 00:09:51,894
He actually lives around the area.

143
00:09:51,894 --> 00:09:53,771
Girl, he’s super rich.

144
00:09:53,771 --> 00:09:55,356
He’s a Lopez-Ledezma.

145
00:09:56,390 --> 00:09:58,183
- What?
- Mhmm.

146
00:10:01,375 --> 00:10:03,186
Speaking of the devil!

147
00:10:03,187 --> 00:10:05,147
Sam, you’re here.

148
00:10:05,898 --> 00:10:08,442
I wish you’d told me so
I could treat you this time.

149
00:10:09,101 --> 00:10:10,936
Come on. It’s fine, Shan.

150
00:10:10,936 --> 00:10:13,522
Anyway, this is my friend, Kierra.

151
00:10:13,522 --> 00:10:15,274
Kierra, this is Shan.

152
00:10:20,487 --> 00:10:22,239
You're too close.

153
00:10:26,702 --> 00:10:28,745
So, how close can we get, Kierra?

154
00:10:30,425 --> 00:10:31,634
What should be our limit?

155
00:10:32,916 --> 00:10:34,126
You tell me.

156
00:10:38,202 --> 00:10:39,680
Should there be a limit?

157
00:10:40,515 --> 00:10:41,758
Crazy idea.

158
00:10:43,635 --> 00:10:46,221
I want to get to know you more.

159
00:10:49,698 --> 00:10:53,076
We’ve only spent a short time together,
but you want to get to know me more?

160
00:10:53,809 --> 00:10:57,115
I don’t know much about you too,
so there should be a limit.

161
00:10:57,730 --> 00:10:59,607
What do you want to know about me?

162
00:11:02,172 --> 00:11:03,172
Wait…

163
00:11:03,614 --> 00:11:05,582
Did I scare you with what I just said?

164
00:11:07,626 --> 00:11:14,257
That maybe I’d want to be in a relationship
with you like your other girls?

165
00:11:17,371 --> 00:11:18,636
Don’t worry.

166
00:11:19,496 --> 00:11:24,335
I’m not even sure if
I can love again anyway. So…

167
00:11:26,120 --> 00:11:27,413
There is a limit.

168
00:11:31,300 --> 00:11:32,594
Yeah.

169
00:11:32,601 --> 00:11:35,063
We know each other.
Right, Kierra?

170
00:11:36,507 --> 00:11:39,761
Oh, shoot.
I forgot I had an appointment.

171
00:11:39,761 --> 00:11:43,286
Shan, Ke, I’ll leave you
two for now, okay?

172
00:11:43,296 --> 00:11:45,871
I need to go. Don’t worry,
I’ll pay for everything.

173
00:11:45,875 --> 00:11:47,165
- Bye, I’ll call you.
- Huh?

174
00:11:48,002 --> 00:11:49,462
Take care, take care.

175
00:11:49,462 --> 00:11:50,463
- Bye!
- Sam, wait—

176
00:11:51,215 --> 00:11:52,175
Bye!

177
00:12:02,904 --> 00:12:03,780
Hi.

178
00:12:06,290 --> 00:12:07,416
Hello.

179
00:12:09,207 --> 00:12:14,985
About the other night,
I can’t remember anything.

180
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:18,713
If I said— If I said something,
I didn’t mean it.

181
00:12:21,906 --> 00:12:23,576
You’re not a good liar, huh?

182
00:12:23,585 --> 00:12:25,033
I really don’t remember.

183
00:12:25,034 --> 00:12:26,411
Okay.

184
00:12:27,245 --> 00:12:29,747
But I’ve just been busy with law school,

185
00:12:29,747 --> 00:12:32,917
so I haven’t been able
to visit the cafe lately.

186
00:12:34,127 --> 00:12:35,127
Who’s asking?

187
00:12:35,712 --> 00:12:37,672
You said you’re busy,
but you can still party, huh?

188
00:12:38,216 --> 00:12:39,674
I saw it on your socials.

189
00:12:40,323 --> 00:12:42,241
That was my friend’s birthday.

190
00:12:42,874 --> 00:12:45,585
Also, thanks for following me back.

191
00:12:48,315 --> 00:12:50,150
I’ll follow you on IG.

192
00:12:51,013 --> 00:12:52,598
I’m following you.

193
00:12:56,604 --> 00:12:57,563
Right?

194
00:12:59,292 --> 00:13:00,251
Follow.

195
00:13:01,461 --> 00:13:02,461
I was drunk.

196
00:13:02,902 --> 00:13:03,861
It doesn’t count.

197
00:13:04,500 --> 00:13:07,711
I have a feeling you missed me.

198
00:13:07,736 --> 00:13:08,904
You wish.

199
00:13:11,052 --> 00:13:13,012
You seem busy, too.

200
00:13:13,907 --> 00:13:15,075
Busy with?

201
00:13:15,906 --> 00:13:17,046
Dating.

202
00:13:17,046 --> 00:13:18,499
Dating?

203
00:13:18,507 --> 00:13:19,550
With who?

204
00:13:20,512 --> 00:13:21,805
That’s not even part of my plan.

205
00:13:22,631 --> 00:13:26,820
I don’t know, maybe the one
who treated you to barbecue?

206
00:13:26,845 --> 00:13:29,514
Or the one who treated
you to kwek-kwek?

207
00:13:31,892 --> 00:13:37,147
But you know what, I know the one who
treats you to froyo is even more handsome.

208
00:13:40,192 --> 00:13:41,067
Let’s go.

209
00:13:41,818 --> 00:13:43,153
Where are you taking me?

210
00:13:43,153 --> 00:13:44,571
We’re going on a date.

211
00:13:45,445 --> 00:13:46,071
Huh?

212
00:13:46,071 --> 00:13:47,445
Come on.

213
00:13:47,460 --> 00:13:48,155
Wait—

214
00:13:48,156 --> 00:13:48,991
Come on.

215
00:13:49,664 --> 00:13:50,206
To—

216
00:13:52,358 --> 00:13:53,901
I hope I got the right flavor now.

217
00:13:56,669 --> 00:13:59,129
Okay. You can ask me five questions.

218
00:13:59,129 --> 00:14:00,798
You can ask me anything.

219
00:14:02,984 --> 00:14:05,237
You own Yesterday’s Coffee?

220
00:14:06,947 --> 00:14:07,820
Yeah.

221
00:14:07,828 --> 00:14:08,682
How?

222
00:14:10,500 --> 00:14:11,918
It used to be my mom’s business.

223
00:14:12,544 --> 00:14:14,337
Eventually, it was transferred to me.

224
00:14:17,304 --> 00:14:20,460
Sam said you’re a Lopez-Ledezma.

225
00:14:21,011 --> 00:14:23,013
Why do you just use Lopez?

226
00:14:29,099 --> 00:14:31,393
They separated, my mom and Alf—

227
00:14:32,003 --> 00:14:33,922
I mean, my dad, when I was young.

228
00:14:34,910 --> 00:14:39,623
But since I lived with my mom,
I used her surname.

229
00:14:43,499 --> 00:14:46,419
Why did you take psychology
as your pre-law course?

230
00:14:48,796 --> 00:14:51,015
Because I’m interested
in how the mind works.

231
00:14:51,023 --> 00:14:58,489
How emotions, feelings,
and thoughts influence a person’s actions.

232
00:15:02,484 --> 00:15:05,789
That’s four.
The next will be your last question.

233
00:15:05,796 --> 00:15:07,623
Think hard about it.

234
00:15:17,500 --> 00:15:18,835
Have we met before?

235
00:15:19,460 --> 00:15:20,753
Have we?

236
00:15:20,757 --> 00:15:24,344
I’m not sure.
You know, the world is small anyway.

237
00:15:26,095 --> 00:15:30,183
So maybe we’ve already met.

238
00:15:35,929 --> 00:15:37,263
That’s mine, by the way.

239
00:15:37,263 --> 00:15:40,202
Sorry. I’ll just get a new straw—

240
00:15:40,210 --> 00:15:41,601
It’s okay.

241
00:15:41,609 --> 00:15:43,730
It’s not like we
haven’t kissed before.

242
00:15:49,615 --> 00:15:50,741
Okay, how about this…

243
00:15:51,990 --> 00:15:53,536
Can I ask you questions now?

244
00:15:53,539 --> 00:15:55,122
Sure, five questions.

245
00:15:57,112 --> 00:15:58,238
First…

246
00:15:59,359 --> 00:16:03,447
Why were you alone the first day
we met at Claremont Hotel?

247
00:16:04,700 --> 00:16:07,359
Second, why did you agree
to have sex with me?

248
00:16:07,383 --> 00:16:08,467
I mean, look at you.

249
00:16:08,926 --> 00:16:12,179
You’re not the type
of girl who just does that.

250
00:16:13,709 --> 00:16:15,461
I was sad back then.

251
00:16:16,757 --> 00:16:18,776
I just wanted to be brave that night.

252
00:16:18,781 --> 00:16:19,320
That’s it.

253
00:16:20,410 --> 00:16:23,329
And I regretted it the very next day.

254
00:16:23,968 --> 00:16:25,820
Why did you pay me that night?

255
00:16:26,937 --> 00:16:28,981
Did you think that was my side hustle?

256
00:16:28,981 --> 00:16:30,399
Huh?

257
00:16:31,687 --> 00:16:34,125
Can I order a breakfast for one?

258
00:16:34,126 --> 00:16:36,662
Can you charge it to Room 237?

259
00:16:37,656 --> 00:16:39,783
You idiot, that was for the food.

260
00:16:45,217 --> 00:16:45,968
Okay.

261
00:16:49,296 --> 00:16:50,548
Last question.

262
00:16:53,405 --> 00:16:54,365
Who is it?

263
00:16:57,126 --> 00:16:59,795
The person you see in your dreams.

264
00:17:04,120 --> 00:17:05,038
Look.

265
00:17:05,898 --> 00:17:08,233
You don’t have to answer
if you’re not comfortable.

266
00:17:12,813 --> 00:17:13,898
My ex.

267
00:17:17,437 --> 00:17:18,897
That’s five questions.

268
00:17:23,506 --> 00:17:25,008
When’s your next shift?

269
00:17:26,712 --> 00:17:27,713
Wow.

270
00:17:28,404 --> 00:17:29,780
You miss me already?

271
00:17:33,968 --> 00:17:37,468
I guess you can have me
back in a week, princess.

272
00:17:38,726 --> 00:17:39,978
I should go.

273
00:17:39,984 --> 00:17:41,652
How will you get home?

274
00:17:44,392 --> 00:17:45,768
Oh right.

275
00:17:49,303 --> 00:17:51,638
Come on, I'll take you home.

276
00:17:56,096 --> 00:17:59,057
It’s so early.
You’ll take me to your condo, Ciandrei?

277
00:18:00,898 --> 00:18:02,582
That’s not what I mean.

278
00:18:02,593 --> 00:18:05,101
What I mean is,
I’ll take you home to your place.

279
00:18:05,117 --> 00:18:08,224
But okay, if you wanna come home to
my place, I mean, I'm still down for that.

280
00:18:09,088 --> 00:18:10,328
Do you wanna see my unit?

281
00:18:10,335 --> 00:18:11,169
I don’t want to.

282
00:18:11,169 --> 00:18:14,009
Why? Because it’s early, right?

283
00:18:14,560 --> 00:18:16,694
We could. We can stay here
for a while until it gets dark.

284
00:18:16,703 --> 00:18:19,549
Or if you want, I can make you
a Sakura latte while waiting.

285
00:18:20,194 --> 00:18:21,112
Damn it.

286
00:18:22,492 --> 00:18:23,618
Let’s go then.

287
00:18:23,618 --> 00:18:25,855
Is this how you invite your FWBs?

288
00:18:26,558 --> 00:18:27,518
Oh.

289
00:18:28,566 --> 00:18:30,401
For the record, this is the first time.

290
00:18:30,414 --> 00:18:34,335
And you're the first girl I've ever
invited to my condo in BGC.

291
00:18:58,671 --> 00:18:59,797
Your mom?

292
00:19:01,095 --> 00:19:02,096
Yeah.

293
00:19:05,851 --> 00:19:08,729
The natural lighting here must
be beautiful in the morning.

294
00:19:09,904 --> 00:19:11,447
To see is to believe.

295
00:19:12,188 --> 00:19:14,691
What if you stay here overnight
so you can find out.

296
00:19:15,786 --> 00:19:17,454
You live here alone?

297
00:19:18,295 --> 00:19:19,338
Uhm—

298
00:19:20,207 --> 00:19:23,085
Technically I’m with you, so…

299
00:19:23,953 --> 00:19:26,416
That was a lame joke.

300
00:19:26,429 --> 00:19:28,707
I’m only here for the Sakura latte.

301
00:19:29,859 --> 00:19:33,237
What if you help me bake, too?

302
00:19:35,406 --> 00:19:37,033
You bake?

303
00:19:37,765 --> 00:19:40,377
That’s quite a reaction. Yeah.

304
00:19:40,382 --> 00:19:41,717
Do I look like I don’t bake?

305
00:19:41,717 --> 00:19:42,676
Yeah.

306
00:19:43,937 --> 00:19:47,561
You know, most of the pastries
at the cafe are my recipes.

307
00:19:47,561 --> 00:19:52,171
We do have an in-house chef who
does the in-house baking, but

308
00:19:52,195 --> 00:19:56,863
since I’ve gotten into baking too,
I bake here from time to time for fun.

309
00:19:58,718 --> 00:20:01,929
For a fuck boy, I wouldn’t think
you’d have soft hobbies.

310
00:20:07,383 --> 00:20:08,791
Here.

311
00:20:08,796 --> 00:20:10,084
Use my apron first.

312
00:20:30,688 --> 00:20:31,730
There. Can I see?

313
00:20:33,918 --> 00:20:34,937
It looks good on you.

314
00:20:35,900 --> 00:20:37,151
Do you have a crush on me?

315
00:20:37,731 --> 00:20:39,274
Is it that obvious?

316
00:20:40,281 --> 00:20:41,365
Liar.

317
00:20:41,796 --> 00:20:42,505
Okay.

318
00:20:42,878 --> 00:20:44,254
Let’s make the batter now.

319
00:21:10,695 --> 00:21:11,530
You can mix it now.

320
00:21:11,530 --> 00:21:12,239
- I’ll mix it?
- Go, yeah.

321
00:21:12,239 --> 00:21:12,948
Okay.

322
00:21:16,066 --> 00:21:17,192
Am I doing it right?

323
00:21:31,921 --> 00:21:32,929
- Oh.
- Oops.

324
00:21:41,296 --> 00:21:43,423
Do you really need to hold my hand?

325
00:21:45,525 --> 00:21:46,776
Unintentional.

326
00:21:49,484 --> 00:21:52,186
Just bake already.
I want to eat cookies.

327
00:21:52,911 --> 00:21:54,204
I’ll mix it.

328
00:22:01,730 --> 00:22:03,569
You’re so messy.

329
00:22:03,578 --> 00:22:06,055
Seems like you’re the one
who needs an apron. Wear this.

330
00:22:06,062 --> 00:22:07,414
No, no. It’s fine.

331
00:22:07,421 --> 00:22:08,505
I’ll just change. Hold on.

332
00:22:10,221 --> 00:22:11,097
Here—

333
00:22:30,492 --> 00:22:31,618
Why?

334
00:22:34,284 --> 00:22:35,284
Wow.

335
00:22:35,914 --> 00:22:38,792
It’s not like you haven’t seen this before.

336
00:22:41,085 --> 00:22:42,503
I’ll just change, okay?

337
00:23:11,515 --> 00:23:12,850
How much is this condo of yours?

338
00:23:14,515 --> 00:23:17,396
I actually don’t know because my mom
bought this when it was cheap.

339
00:23:17,406 --> 00:23:21,320
So for sure the price has gone up a lot.

340
00:23:21,335 --> 00:23:23,624
Your mom is so business-minded.

341
00:23:23,632 --> 00:23:26,380
I’m sure she has a lot of investments
that have turned profitable by now.

342
00:23:28,804 --> 00:23:29,805
What about you?

343
00:23:30,441 --> 00:23:32,568
Tell me about your family.

344
00:23:34,085 --> 00:23:34,952
Oh…

345
00:23:34,968 --> 00:23:38,148
Apologies, if you can’t
answer the question, it’s okay.

346
00:23:38,156 --> 00:23:40,044
No, I’m good with my parents.

347
00:23:40,820 --> 00:23:43,327
My dad works for my uncle.
He’s an artist.

348
00:23:43,351 --> 00:23:45,533
My mom owns a school. That’s it.

349
00:23:46,201 --> 00:23:47,202
That’s it.

350
00:23:47,991 --> 00:23:50,244
You, what about your family?

351
00:23:54,484 --> 00:23:56,710
It’s raining hard.

352
00:23:56,718 --> 00:23:58,678
Shit. How will I get home?

353
00:23:59,945 --> 00:24:01,816
You can wait out the rain here if you want.

354
00:24:01,835 --> 00:24:04,976
If you want, you can sleep here.
I have a guest room anyway.

355
00:24:05,994 --> 00:24:11,867
And you can also play with my game console,
but I have to go to my room.

356
00:24:11,882 --> 00:24:13,171
I need to study.

357
00:24:13,179 --> 00:24:14,828
Go ahead. Don’t mind me.

358
00:24:14,843 --> 00:24:16,511
I don’t want you to fail because of me.

359
00:24:17,700 --> 00:24:21,621
Nah, I have a feeling
I’ll be studying inspired.

360
00:24:24,258 --> 00:24:26,803
You talk a lot. Go study already.

361
00:24:27,863 --> 00:24:29,198
I’ll be back.

362
00:24:52,000 --> 00:24:54,002
Oh shit! Luna.

363
00:24:54,633 --> 00:24:57,621
<i>Where are you? It’s raining hard!</i>
<i>Are you home yet?</i>

364
00:25:00,835 --> 00:25:04,684
<i>I ended up staying at Sam’s place.</i>
<i>I’m sleeping here.</i>

365
00:25:07,348 --> 00:25:10,101
<i>I’m with Sam right now.</i>

366
00:25:12,710 --> 00:25:14,221
<i>Who are you with, huh?</i>

367
00:25:14,226 --> 00:25:15,727
<i>Is that your new boyfriend?</i>

368
00:25:15,727 --> 00:25:17,187
<i>You want me to beat him up?</i>

369
00:25:19,765 --> 00:25:21,308
You’re such a dumbass, Ke.

370
00:25:21,859 --> 00:25:23,945
That’s the worst excuse ever.

371
00:25:24,791 --> 00:25:26,293
You’re gonna be in so much
trouble when you get home.

372
00:26:40,706 --> 00:26:41,665
Shan?

373
00:26:46,905 --> 00:26:49,282
Oh. He fell asleep.

374
00:27:04,219 --> 00:27:05,429
Ciandrei.

375
00:27:09,620 --> 00:27:10,788
Okay.

376
00:27:12,891 --> 00:27:14,184
Five minutes.

377
00:27:55,872 --> 00:27:56,967
Good morning.

378
00:27:57,781 --> 00:28:00,742
Sorry, I fell asleep in your room.

379
00:28:02,109 --> 00:28:02,985
You know,

380
00:28:03,796 --> 00:28:07,998
it’s my first time sleeping over with a girl
without ending up in the same bed as her.

381
00:28:09,732 --> 00:28:10,817
That’s fine.

382
00:28:11,812 --> 00:28:13,647
You slept so deeply.

383
00:28:14,314 --> 00:28:15,444
You were even snoring.

384
00:28:16,391 --> 00:28:17,809
Jerk! Seriously?

385
00:28:19,837 --> 00:28:22,493
Hey. Aren’t you— Are you serious?

386
00:28:23,198 --> 00:28:24,449
I’m just kidding.

387
00:28:26,328 --> 00:28:27,579
So annoying.

388
00:28:28,204 --> 00:28:31,666
But yeah, I really slept soundly.

389
00:28:36,421 --> 00:28:37,023
Let me help you.

390
00:28:37,031 --> 00:28:37,966
No, no. It’s okay.

391
00:28:37,968 --> 00:28:38,827
Just sit.

392
00:28:38,843 --> 00:28:41,218
This is almost done.
This is the last one. Come on.

393
00:28:41,234 --> 00:28:43,445
I’ll just make you some coffee.

394
00:28:44,487 --> 00:28:47,073
You’ll make coffee for a barista?

395
00:28:47,073 --> 00:28:49,218
Excuse me, I know how to make coffee.

396
00:28:49,218 --> 00:28:52,388
Once you taste my coffee,
maybe you’ll want to close down your cafe.

397
00:29:41,132 --> 00:29:42,967
Okay, fine. It’s not good.
Stop drinking it.

398
00:29:42,967 --> 00:29:44,302
No, no. It’s fine.

399
00:29:45,409 --> 00:29:48,370
Maybe it was just a bad espresso shot.

400
00:29:48,370 --> 00:29:50,796
And your milk-steaming, maybe...

401
00:29:50,796 --> 00:29:55,301
it was a bit off but overall,

402
00:29:55,991 --> 00:29:56,867
decent.

403
00:29:57,915 --> 00:29:59,542
Thanks for the critique.

404
00:30:00,241 --> 00:30:03,994
Yeah, I’m never making
coffee for a barista again.

405
00:30:07,609 --> 00:30:09,194
Oh shit! I need to go home.

406
00:30:09,820 --> 00:30:11,218
My cousin’s gonna kill me.

407
00:30:11,219 --> 00:30:12,780
I’ll take you home.

408
00:30:12,796 --> 00:30:14,398
No. No need.

409
00:30:14,405 --> 00:30:16,064
Are you sure?

410
00:30:16,070 --> 00:30:17,614
Okay then, how about this…

411
00:30:18,480 --> 00:30:20,190
I'll give you one condition.

412
00:30:20,957 --> 00:30:23,835
Meet me in Yesterday.
8PM, Wednesday.

413
00:30:25,011 --> 00:30:25,845
Fine.

414
00:30:26,513 --> 00:30:28,014
See you in Yesterday.

415
00:31:05,113 --> 00:31:06,327
Where were you?

416
00:31:06,351 --> 00:31:08,951
Why weren’t you answering
my calls and messages?

417
00:31:09,646 --> 00:31:11,481
You met with your boyfriend, didn’t you?

418
00:31:15,002 --> 00:31:16,378
Well?

419
00:31:17,237 --> 00:31:18,363
Sorry.

420
00:31:19,195 --> 00:31:22,006
I just played with his game console.

421
00:31:22,023 --> 00:31:24,826
And then I fell asleep, no joke.

422
00:31:25,495 --> 00:31:27,288
Why didn’t you answer my call?

423
00:31:27,786 --> 00:31:28,954
My phone died.

424
00:31:29,601 --> 00:31:33,062
Can you stop asking me questions?
I made it home alive, didn’t I?

425
00:31:33,070 --> 00:31:35,107
Okay, fine. Fine.

426
00:31:36,576 --> 00:31:38,995
Just please, tell me next time, okay?

427
00:31:40,726 --> 00:31:46,040
By the way, Sevi and Theo are
inviting us to go to Antipolo on Wednesday.

428
00:31:46,064 --> 00:31:47,816
They found this good restaurant.

429
00:31:48,296 --> 00:31:49,422
Wednesday?

430
00:31:49,422 --> 00:31:50,382
Yeah.

431
00:31:50,382 --> 00:31:52,632
We’ll be done with school early anyway.

432
00:31:52,648 --> 00:31:54,734
I can’t. I have something to do.

433
00:31:56,213 --> 00:31:57,506
What do you have to do?

434
00:31:58,429 --> 00:31:59,221
Just something.

435
00:31:59,793 --> 00:32:02,587
What? What’s this, “just something”?

436
00:32:02,587 --> 00:32:04,297
You’re gonna be
with your boyfriend, aren’t you?

437
00:32:04,297 --> 00:32:05,882
He’s not my boyfriend.

438
00:32:05,882 --> 00:32:07,500
He’s not your boyfriend?

439
00:32:07,507 --> 00:32:09,217
You’re meeting someone
who’s not your boyfriend?

440
00:32:09,226 --> 00:32:10,227
You know, you—

441
00:32:10,227 --> 00:32:12,480
You ask so many questions,
I said he’s not my boyfriend.

442
00:32:12,980 --> 00:32:14,023
Ke!

443
00:32:16,617 --> 00:32:18,035
Not your boyfriend? As if!

444
00:32:38,734 --> 00:32:40,711
Why am I trying to look nice?

445
00:32:40,726 --> 00:32:42,269
We’re just having coffee.

446
00:32:47,234 --> 00:32:50,404
I guess I can still look cute
even if it’s just for coffee.

447
00:33:57,429 --> 00:34:01,684
<i> Hi. I’m at the cafe already.</i>
<i>Are you coming?</i>

448
00:34:07,398 --> 00:34:09,381
Hi. Is this seat taken?

449
00:34:09,382 --> 00:34:10,300
Yeah, sorry.

450
00:34:25,021 --> 00:34:26,021
<i>Where are you?</i>

451
00:34:27,257 --> 00:34:29,275
<i>Can you at least give</i>
<i>me an update, please?</i>

452
00:34:49,030 --> 00:34:50,088
<i>Are we still meeting up?</i>

453
00:36:28,484 --> 00:36:30,069
I strangled him.

454
00:36:35,096 --> 00:36:37,348
I didn’t even realize
how tightly I’d held him.

455
00:36:39,785 --> 00:36:42,162
And how did you
come back to your senses?

456
00:36:42,782 --> 00:36:43,825
Nothing.

457
00:36:44,694 --> 00:36:47,030
Someone came, so I let go.

458
00:36:51,630 --> 00:36:53,423
I don’t want to be like him.

459
00:36:54,092 --> 00:36:55,260
Your father?

460
00:36:59,123 --> 00:37:04,128
I feel like I’m so scared
right now of becoming like him.

461
00:37:05,103 --> 00:37:08,857
To the point where I can’t sleep
at night thinking about it.

462
00:37:10,992 --> 00:37:12,744
I don’t wanna be like him.

463
00:37:14,878 --> 00:37:16,714
I don’t wanna hurt anyone.

464
00:37:21,593 --> 00:37:23,721
I don’t want to hurt her.

465
00:37:24,502 --> 00:37:27,339
Her, your sister?

466
00:37:29,007 --> 00:37:31,134
I would never hurt my sister,

467
00:37:33,499 --> 00:37:35,376
but she’s not who I’m talking about.

468
00:37:40,297 --> 00:37:41,673
I met someone.

469
00:37:51,900 --> 00:37:53,484
A beautiful girl.

470
00:37:55,202 --> 00:37:56,787
And she wants to get to know me.

471
00:37:58,898 --> 00:38:00,900
And that scares you?

472
00:38:05,408 --> 00:38:07,743
I don’t want her to see this side of me.

473
00:38:09,380 --> 00:38:10,965
I’m sure she’ll stay away.

474
00:38:17,597 --> 00:38:20,141
I just want to apologize
for what happened.

475
00:38:21,848 --> 00:38:23,225
I know I hurt you.

476
00:38:23,714 --> 00:38:26,842
That was a long time ago, Shan.
We’re fine now, aren’t we?

477
00:38:26,842 --> 00:38:28,260
What’s wrong with you?

478
00:38:28,925 --> 00:38:30,176
Yeah, I know but—

479
00:38:30,176 --> 00:38:32,386
You’re feeling guilty, aren’t you? Why?

480
00:38:33,202 --> 00:38:35,079
Are you already in love with someone?

481
00:38:40,644 --> 00:38:42,070
You’re in love, bro.

482
00:38:42,647 --> 00:38:44,124
Bro, chill.

483
00:38:44,128 --> 00:38:45,963
Me? Fall in love?

484
00:38:46,910 --> 00:38:47,909
Never.

485
00:38:48,336 --> 00:38:50,370
You know what,
that’s what everyone’s been saying.

486
00:38:51,101 --> 00:38:52,644
But that’s just not me.

487
00:38:54,104 --> 00:38:59,300
I mean, for you to go out
of your way to apologize

488
00:38:59,308 --> 00:39:01,766
to every girl you’ve hurt before.

489
00:39:03,614 --> 00:39:06,116
I’m sensing you’re afraid of karma.

490
00:39:08,486 --> 00:39:11,322
All right, all right.
Whatever you say, bro.

491
00:39:11,969 --> 00:39:12,720
Bye.

492
00:39:13,305 --> 00:39:14,556
Okay.

493
00:39:15,113 --> 00:39:17,324
Okay. Just call me anytime as always.

494
00:39:17,324 --> 00:39:19,409
Bye, lover boy.

495
00:39:25,341 --> 00:39:26,405
And maybe…

496
00:39:27,145 --> 00:39:28,397
Maybe it’s right.

497
00:39:30,003 --> 00:39:32,003
Maybe it’s right that
she shouldn’t know me.

498
00:39:33,156 --> 00:39:35,450
Why do you say that, Shan?

499
00:39:36,413 --> 00:39:40,527
Cause if I’m like this,
I’m no good for her.

500
00:39:41,415 --> 00:39:44,043
Shan, you made a mistake once,

501
00:39:44,809 --> 00:39:47,902
but that doesn’t mean
you’re like your dad now.

502
00:39:49,190 --> 00:39:51,991
Just the fact that you’re
here means that you’re

503
00:39:51,995 --> 00:39:54,557
actively doing something
to not be like him.

504
00:39:55,288 --> 00:39:59,084
You can’t avoid everyone
who wants to get to know you.

505
00:40:02,474 --> 00:40:04,393
Why don’t you give this a chance?

506
00:40:09,193 --> 00:40:11,195
Give yourself a chance.

507
00:40:35,699 --> 00:40:36,992
Sweet dreams.

508
00:40:38,180 --> 00:40:39,682
No nightmares tonight.

509
00:41:07,886 --> 00:41:10,847
Shan, why are you afraid to open up?

510
00:41:14,449 --> 00:41:16,761
Who was that guy the other night?

511
00:41:16,769 --> 00:41:18,925
How did you meet that person from Taft?

512
00:41:18,925 --> 00:41:21,206
How did you know he went to Taft?

513
00:41:21,214 --> 00:41:23,995
This happened before Kalix...

514
00:41:24,003 --> 00:41:26,255
Ke! I’m so sorry, Ke!

515
00:41:28,152 --> 00:41:29,207
Let me make it up to you.

516
00:41:29,214 --> 00:41:30,924
And then are you just going
to stand me up again?

517
00:41:32,503 --> 00:41:34,492
You can say you’re not ready yet.

518
00:41:34,503 --> 00:41:37,116
You know, if he truly
cares about you, he’ll wait.

519
00:41:37,803 --> 00:41:40,598
You can ask the other person
that you need more time.

520
00:41:44,815 --> 00:41:45,733
Are you going to see him?

521
00:41:47,232 --> 00:41:48,775
Are you sure? Are you ready?

522
00:41:50,019 --> 00:41:51,105
Sorry, Ke—

523
00:41:51,113 --> 00:41:52,469
I’m just going to the restroom.

524
00:41:52,472 --> 00:41:54,429
- I’ll be right back.
- Okay.

525
00:41:54,433 --> 00:41:55,888
Shan! Are you on a date?

526
00:41:55,894 --> 00:41:58,433
Who is she? Introduce me.

527
00:41:58,437 --> 00:42:02,433
I think you should introduce me
to your new partner, don’t you think?
